%description:

The downlink budget, end to end, against the closed form.

The unit tests stop at the path-loss term and the fingerprints only hash the
consequences, so nothing checks that the model assembles a received signal
level correctly out of its ingredients. With fading, shadowing and every
interference contribution switched off, an omnidirectional antenna and a fixed
LOS state, the SINR the UE reports is a sum of constants and one path loss:

    SINR = txPower - PL(d) + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss - thermalNoise - noiseFigure

Every term but PL is a parameter of the scenario. PL comes from
pathloss_reference.py -- the independent transcription of the 3GPP formulas
that grades the path-loss unit tests -- so the two layers are held to one
statement of what TR 38.901 requires, and cannot drift apart. That join is the
point of the test as much as the arithmetic is.

The UE is swept over five distances, which also carries the second claim: the
budget has to fall monotonically with distance. The sweep straddles the
breakpoint distance (about 120 m for this geometry at 2 GHz), so both branches
of the UMi LOS formula are exercised.

A note on the geometry, because it is a trap rather than a detail. The heights
that enter the formula are the nodebHeight and ueHeight parameters, while the
distance comes from the nodes' actual coordinates. They are independent
inputs: leave initialZ unset and the model computes a path loss for a 10 m
base station over a distance measured as though it stood on the ground. The
configuration below keeps them consistent and the grader checks that it does,
because an inconsistent scenario would not fail -- it would quietly grade a
different geometry.

%extraargs: -c LinkBudget

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config LinkBudget]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count

############### The sweep ##############
# Straddles the breakpoint distance, so both branches of the LOS formula run.
**.ueDistance = ${d = 50, 100, 200, 400, 800}

############### Geometry ##############
# initialZ and the height parameters have to agree: the first sets the distance
# the model measures, the second the heights the formula uses.
*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 450m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 10m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[0].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[0].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 450m + ${d}m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one path loss and nothing else ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 10m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

############### The budget terms, stated rather than inherited ##############
# A physics test should not inherit the numbers it is asserting about: these are
# the NED defaults today, written down so that changing a default makes this
# test disagree with the model loudly instead of moving silently with it.
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
**.antennGainEnB = 18dBi
**.antennaGainUe = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
**.ueNoiseFigure = 7dBm

############### Traffic, only to make the UE report ##############
*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 1
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=10 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
